## ⚠ Production activation is blocked on DNS, independently of everything above

**Site mail currently fails DKIM at Gmail.** Read from `Business OS\ANDREW-REVIEW\2026-09-05\SITE-MAIL-AUTH-READ.md` (Gimli, 2026-09-05, Gmail RAW headers, verified live by that desk — **read from his document by me, not re-verified**):

> `dkim=permerror (no key for signature) header.i=@braveheartspublishing.com header.s=default`
> `dmarc=fail (p=NONE sp=NONE dis=NONE)`

Root cause recorded there: the DKIM public key sits as a TXT record on the **apex**, while the signature says `s=default`, so verifiers look at `default._domainkey.braveheartspublishing.com` and find nothing. SPF passes but is not aligned. Delivery survives only because the policy is `p=none`.

⛔ **Do not switch `bhp_review_ask_enabled` on in production before that record is published.** This engine sends through `wp_mail` on the same path. The note is repeated in the engine file's header so a future deploy cannot miss it.

