# ROUND 3 — 1.19.364 · SEAL 977 (2026-09-05, CYCLE179-LD-REVIEW-SEQ)

**Artefact:** `C:\BHP\_prod-candidates\cycle179-review-seq\brave-hearts-theme-1.19.364-review-seq.zip`
**md5:** `cfbaf4eaecb42a863e7d65bf0a145691` · 727 files · 35.6 MB uncompressed
**Local commit (feature branch `feature/cycle179-review-seq-1.19.362`, NOT pushed):** `85a937b`

## The two staging failures, and what actually caused each

**1. `A due WEB order declines copy_not_approved` — got `not_due`. THE FIXTURE WAS WRONG, THE ENGINE WAS RIGHT.**
`$bhp_rs_w1` was built **9 days** old. The web lane's touch-1 delay is `BHP_REVIEW_ASK_WEB_DELAY_DAYS` = **10**. The order was genuinely not due and the engine said so correctly. The probe is now built **12 days** old and the assertion means what it was written to mean.

⛔ **The web delay was NOT changed to 7, and that is a deliberate refusal.** Andrew's seal 977 reads *"Then the 7 day review ask for the website and 10day for multiple books"*, which has two honest readings — 7/10 in every lane, or 7/10 in the VISIT lane with *"for the website"* naming the destination. Merry's `CYCLE179-MKT-REVIEW-SEQ-V2.md` §4 takes the second reading explicitly and marks the web timing *"still an inference, not a seal"*, carried as open conflict **CYCLE179-MKT-34**. Editing a constant would have settled an open conflict by fiat. **It goes to Andrew.**

**2. `An order with no chapter book declines unresolved_merge_slot` — got `(empty)`. A REAL AND SERIOUS DEFECT, AND THE SUITE FOUND IT.**

`bhp_review_ask_copy()` ended with `return bhp_review_ask_merge_copy( $copy, $order );`. `bhp_review_ask_decline_reason()` then handed that **already-substituted** array to `bhp_review_ask_merge_is_complete()`, which looks for **unresolved slots** with `strpos( $blob, '{BookTitle}' )`. Every slot had already been replaced — with the empty string, for this order — so the search found nothing, `continue`d, and returned `true`.

⛔⛔ **The unresolved-slot gate has therefore never fired, on any order, in any environment, since it was written.** It is not that it fired late; an email reading *"Thank you for picking up  at ."* was one qualifying order away the whole time. The only things that kept it off a parent were the master switch being off and the unapproved copy.

**The fix is a separation, not a patch.** `bhp_review_ask_copy_raw()` returns the unmerged set and the gates read it; `bhp_review_ask_copy()` merges and the renderer reads that. A gate that inspects post-substitution text can never see a slot, so the same class of mistake cannot be made again.

## Why `wp bhp review-ask dry` reported examined 0 — and what now prints

**I could not observe staging's database from here** (no SSH this session, `CYCLE179-LD-43`). So instead of guessing, the dry run now **describes the pool before it walks it** and prints the reason:

- A `POOL:` line counting shop orders by status (`any`, `completed`, `processing`, `on-hold`, `pending`, `cancelled`, `refunded`, `failed`) via a **count-only** `return => ids` query that loads no order objects.
- When the pool is empty, an explicit three-way explanation: **no shop orders in any status** (they are not in this copy of the database) · **orders exist but none is `completed`** (the candidate query is correctly skipping them — the engine anchors on `date_completed` and cannot schedule an order that never completed) · **or completed orders exist and the query still returned none**, which points at HPOS, an order-type filter, or a plugin's `wc_get_orders` filter.
- **Per skipped order, on a dry run only:** `DRY: SKIP order N | <lane> lane | K chapter book(s) | next touch T | due YYYY-MM-DD | REASON: <slug>`, plus the same facts as a row in `$summary['orders']` with `result => skipped`.

⛔ **The aggregate `declined` counts are unchanged** — this adds detail, it does not replace the summary. **No email address, name or order total is printed by any line.** Live runs stay quiet, because a live run walks the same orders every morning.

⚠ **The answer to "are the 16 visit orders present on staging?" is what the POOL line will say on the next run. I have not asserted it, because I have not seen it.**

## What else 1.19.364 changes

| # | Change | Where |
|---|---|---|
| 2 | **Touch 2 is +4 days, not +7** (Andrew: *"If no reviews we ask 4 days later"*). Constant, filter default, the touch-2 set's own `delay_days` interlock and the suite moved together. Superseded 7 preserved in comments at every site | `inc/review-ask-email.php` |
| 3 | **Star row.** Five links, 5→1, one per rating, labels **shared with the site form** through the new `bhp_review_star_labels()` — one declaration, two readers, so the email and the page cannot drift. Table-based, inline-styled, `★` glyphs (no images to block), **every cell carries its visible label**, glyph `aria-hidden`. Plain-text part carries five text links in the same order | `inc/reviews.php`, both `woocommerce/emails/…bhp-review-ask.php` |
| 3 | **Signed pre-fill token.** HMAC-SHA256 over order id + email + product key + absolute expiry, keyed on `wp_salt('auth')`, URL-safe base64, **30-day** TTL, `hash_equals()` comparison. ⛔ Trusted for pre-fill and nothing else — no auth, no moderation skip, no "verified" mark. A token minted for one title does not pre-fill another title's form | `inc/reviews.php` |
| 3 | **The review page accepts both.** `?rating=` sanitised to an integer 1–5 (`ctype_digit` on the raw string — `5.0`, `+5`, `5abc`, `rating[]=5` and `<script>` all resolve to 0, silently). ⛔ **A failed submission always outranks the URL**, so a validation error cannot silently rewrite the reader's own 3 stars into the 5 still sitting in their address bar. Textarea autofocuses **only** when a star genuinely arrived. **No parameter, no token → exactly the 1.19.262 form** | `template-parts/reviews/review-form.php` |
| 4 | **Day 0 is a warm note that asks for nothing.** `_default` replaced with Merry's V2 §1 body verbatim, slots `{ParentFirstName}` `{SchoolName}` `{BookTitle(s)}` `{VisitLine}`, with a merge resolver. `{VisitLine}` is read from the visit record and **never auto-filled**; empty renders nothing and the email closes up around it. Superseded set preserved verbatim in comments with its date | `inc/visit-completed-email.php` |
| 5 | **One destination.** The Amazon sentence is gone from touch 1 **and from both day-0 sets**, each preserved verbatim in a comment. Merry decoded the V6 bookmark QR first-hand: it resolves to `amazon.com/review/create-review`, so those sentences named the exact second destination Andrew removed. `CYCLE179-LD-40` is closed by this | both files |
| 6 | **The copy gate is now absolute in the day-0 file too.** `approved` there previously *reported and did not gate* — its own docblock said so. With `{ParentFirstName}` now in that body, an unapproved set reaching a parent would render literal curly braces. `bhp_visit_email_string()` and `bhp_visit_email_body()` return ''/`array()` for an unapproved or unresolvable set, which routes the order to WooCommerce's ordinary completed-order email. **The customer still gets their notice. Nobody gets placeholder text** | `inc/visit-completed-email.php` |

