# ROUND 12 — 1.19.373 — 2026-09-05

**Agent:** `lead-developer` (Aragorn), subagent of `chief-of-staff`.
**Lock:** `Business OS\LOCKS\lead-developer-CYCLE179-LD-REVIEW-SEQ-R12.lock`.
**Acquired** 2026-09-05T14:33-0600, **released** at the timestamp in the lock
file — both read off this machine's clock with `date`, first-hand.
**Pre-edit backups:** `Business OS\LOCKS\_pre-edit-backups-2026-09-05-cycle179-ld-review-seq-r12\`.
**Commit:** `220d52c` on `feature/cycle179-review-seq-1.19.362`. Local only.

## 0. The one-line answer

The 1.19.372 H1 failure was **not a regex bug — the filter ran at a stage the
failing assertion never sees**, and that is fixed at the render stage; seal 1007
now reaches the legacy 21-day set; the Adams heroes ship and are mapped; the
general hero became one constant whose default deliberately did not move.

## 1. Item 1 — THE EMPTY H1 BAND. The diagnosis is the deliverable.

### What was observed

`rs372-day0.html`, read byte-for-byte at this desk on 2026-09-05, still carries:

```html
<td id="header_wrapper" style="padding: 20px 32px 0; display: block;">
    <h1 style='font-weight: 700; line-height: 120%; margin: 0; color: #342f28;
        background-color: inherit; text-align: left;
        font-family: "EB Garamond",Georgia,"Times New Roman",serif;
        letter-spacing: normal; font-size: 30px;' bgcolor="inherit"></h1>
</td>
```

All four 1.19.372 renders (`day0`, `touch1`, `touch2`, `web1`) carry it.

### Why 1.19.372 could not have worked

⛔ **`woocommerce_mail_content` is applied inside `WC_Email::send()`**, to
`style_inline( $message )` — the last moment before `wp_mail()`. But the failing
assertion reads `$bhp_rs_d0_email->get_content_html()`, and every rendered
document in `REVIEW-SEQ-STAGING\` is captured from `get_content_html()` /
`get_content()`. Those run **earlier** and never pass through that filter.

⭐ So 1.19.372's regexes were fine — `#<h1\b[^>]*>\s*</h1>#i` does match that
element, and the wrapper's `id` does precede a double-quoted `style`. The filter
simply never saw the string the test was holding. **A filter on the wrong stage
is indistinguishable from a broken regex until you ask which string the failing
assertion actually contains.**

### Two further defects found while the diagnosis was open

1. ⛔ **The padding zeroing returned early when no `<h1>` had just been
   removed** (`if ( null === $stripped || ! $count ) { return $content; }`).
   The moment the element started being removed earlier in the pipeline, the
   late filter would have left the visible 20px band standing — the fix would
   have "worked" and still looked wrong.
2. ⛔ **The wrapper patterns hard-coded `style="`.** `rs372-day0.html` proves
   Emogrifier emits `style='…'` with **single** quotes whenever the value holds
   a quoted font stack. On an inlined document those patterns would have missed
   the H1's own attribute, and on any build where the wrapper is single-quoted
   they would have missed the padding too.

### The fix

- `bhp_email_header_without_empty_band( $email_heading, $email )` buffers
  `do_action( 'woocommerce_email_header', … )` and passes the fragment through
  `bhp_email_strip_empty_heading()`. Both templates this theme already overrides
  call it. **The element is therefore gone from `get_content_html()`** — what
  the suite reads, what the staging renders capture, and what the mailer gets.
- ⛔ **This is not an override of `emails/email-header.php`**, which this theme
  forbids. The action fires unchanged, with the same two arguments; every other
  listener runs in its normal order; only the assembled output is processed.
- ⚠ **The fallback is the original line.** If `inc/transactional-emails.php` is
  not loaded, both templates render exactly as before 1.19.373.
- The late `woocommerce_mail_content` registration is **kept**, belt-and-braces,
  for any WooCommerce email rendering an empty heading through a template this
  theme does not override.
- The padding rule is now the honest one: **header wrapper present AND no `<h1>`
  anywhere in the document → padding goes to zero**, regardless of whether this
  call is what removed it.
- The wrapper tag is rewritten by `preg_replace_callback` →
  `bhp_email_zero_header_padding()`: strips whatever `style` attribute exists in
  either quote style, writes back `style="padding: 0;"`. Attribute order,
  quoting, and the attribute's very existence are all no longer assumed.

### Evidence — and exactly what kind it is

⚠ **There is no PHP on this machine** (`php -v` → command not found). Nothing
was executed as PHP. What *was* done: the two functions were **transliterated
