## 0. The one-line answer

Both 1.19.373 failures were the same defect class — **an assertion reading a
different object from the one the code builds** — and both are fixed in the
source rather than in the test. Seal 1027 lands (the general hero is the Adams
library). Seal 1025's day-0 shipping row is shortened and left-aligned **without
minting a single word of new customer-facing copy**. ⛔ Nothing was run as PHP.

## 1. Item 1a — review-seq 484/1, at the root

**The failure, verbatim:** *"The general row is driven by the constant, not by a
second literal"*.

⛔ **The assertion was right and the map was right.** The map literal lived
inside `bhp_review_ask_hero()`. From outside that function the only handle was
`apply_filters( 'bhp_review_ask_hero_map', array() )` — and a filter with no
registered callback returns the default it was handed, which was `array()`. **The
suite was asserting against an empty array.** The table was unreadable, not
incorrect, and an unreadable table cannot be guarded.

**The fix is in `inc/review-ask-email.php`, not in the suite.** New function
`bhp_review_ask_hero_map()` holds the `define()` and the table; the resolver
calls it; the suite calls it. One place a hero filename can be written.

⭐ **The filter name, its signature and its default rows are unchanged**, so any
`bhp_review_ask_hero_map` callback written against 1.19.370–373 keeps working
byte-identically. What moved is where the default array is built.

⭐ **Two more instances of the same defect were found and fixed while the
diagnosis was open**, both in `tests/test-cycle179-review-seq.php`:

| Was | Why it was wrong |
|---|---|
| `strpos( $bhp_rs_html, 'hero-read-aloud-general.jpg' )` | a hard-coded filename standing in for "the general hero" — it would have failed on seal 1027 while describing nothing actually wrong. Now reads `BHP_EMAIL_GENERAL_HERO`. |
| `strpos( $bhp_rs_html, 'Caption: A morning read-aloud' )` | a hard-coded caption sentence. The two general candidates carry **different** caption sentences (the Dallas file's is prefixed `Caption:`, the Adams one's is not) because those strings are Legolas's transcriptions of what is baked into each photograph. Now compares against `bhp_review_ask_hero_alt( BHP_EMAIL_GENERAL_HERO )`. |
| `$bhp_rs_h_map = apply_filters( 'bhp_review_ask_hero_map', array() )` at the DES-31 guard | the same empty-array read. That guard was passing against nothing. Now reads the function, and a new assertion checks the map actually has rows to guard. |

## 2. Item 1b — cycle169 124/1, at the root

