# ROUND 14 — 1.19.375 — 2026-09-05 — seal 1032, every book in the paragraph

**Agent:** lead-developer (Aragorn), subagent of chief-of-staff (Gandalf)
**Lock:** `Business OS\LOCKS\lead-developer-CYCLE179-LD-REVIEW-SEQ-R14.lock`
**Branch:** `feature/cycle179-review-seq-1.19.362` · **Commit:** `82ade70`
**Started 15:12 MDT, finished 15:23 MDT** (machine clock, `date`, first-hand)

## 0. The one-line answer

`{BookTitle}` now resolves to **every chapter book on the order**, joined by the
day-0 join that was **extracted rather than copied**; a new slot
`{FirstBookTitle}` carries the one book the five-star row can actually rate, and
the send gate learned it. One-book orders — which CYCLE179-MKT-32 says is most of
them — render **byte-identically to 1.19.374**.

## 1. The founder rule, verbatim

Andrew Signore, 2026-09-05, **⛔ RELAYED through Gandalf, not heard first-hand**:

> *"I also assume the 'mariana trench' is just a holder for 1 book and will be
> the book that was purchased in its place on production and if its multiple
> books all the books listed in the paragraph"*

Recorded as **seal 1032**.

## 2. What was actually wrong

`{BookTitle}` resolved through `bhp_review_ask_book_title()`, which returns the
**first** chapter book on the order. A parent who bought all three read:

> "Your reader has had The Mariana Trench for a week and a half now."

…while looking at three books. ⚠ The engine already **knew** the order held more
than one book — that is precisely what selects the +10 day delay
(`BHP_REVIEW_ASK_VISIT_DELAY_MULTI_BOOK`) over +7. The delay knew; the sentence
did not.

## 3. Item 1 — the list, and why it was EXTRACTED and not written

`bhp_review_ask_book_title_list( $order )` is **the day-0 join, moved**. It has
shipped inside `bhp_visit_email_merge_values()` since 1.19.364 under Merry's slot
table (*"One title verbatim, or a natural list for two or more: The Mariana
Trench and Mount Everest"*). `inc/visit-completed-email.php` now **calls** it.

⛔ **Why not a second implementation.** The day-0 email and the +7 ask describe
the **same order**, days apart, to the **same parent**. Two copies of a join
drift, and the parent is the one who notices. §17 asserts the two lanes produce
the identical string at one, two and three books.

⚠ **Byte-identical output**: same loop, same `implode( ', ' )`, same trailing
`" and "`, **including the absent serial comma** ("A, B and C", not "A, B, and
C"). That is the day-0 behaviour Andrew has already read on the staging
test-sends; it was not restyled on an engineer's preference.

**Rendered, all three shapes** (⚠ transliterated to Python and run — evidence
about the strings, **not** about the PHP):

| Books | `{BookTitle}` |
|---|---|
| 1 | The Mariana Trench |
| 2 | The Mariana Trench and Mount Everest |
| 3 | The Mariana Trench, Mount Everest and The Amazon |

## 4. Item 2 — `{FirstBookTitle}`, and why it is not a convenience

The star row has **one destination** (seal 977, *"I want one destination not 2"*)
and a review page exists **per title**. So the row and its caption can only ever
be about one book. Without a second slot, the caption would have become:

> "Tap a star to rate The Mariana Trench and Mount Everest."

— an instruction the row **cannot carry out**.

- `{BookTitle}` → `bhp_review_ask_book_title_list()` (the list)
- `{FirstBookTitle}` → `bhp_review_ask_book_title()` (unchanged function, unchanged return value, **new slot**)
- Caption, all three sets: `Tap a star to rate {FirstBookTitle}.`
- `links[0]['url']` → `{ReviewLink}` → still the first book's page. §17 asserts caption and destination name the **same** book.

⛔ **The gate learned the slot.** `bhp_review_ask_merge_is_complete()` now checks
`{FirstBookTitle}`. Leaving it off would have been **the 1.19.363 defect in a new
spelling**: the caption is the only string carrying it, so *"Tap a star to
rate ."* would have shipped while the gate looked only for `{BookTitle}`.
Asserted with a synthetic set carrying **only** that slot, so it cannot pass on
the back of `{BookTitle}` or `{ReviewLink}`.

⛔ **The substring hazard, checked not assumed.** Both tokens are replaced in one
`str_replace()` pass. Neither is a substring of the other — inside
`{FirstBookTitle}` the character before `BookTitle}` is `t`, not `{` — so the
substitution is order-independent. §17 asserts it against a probe string so a
future rename cannot break it silently.

## 5. Item 3 — agreement, sentence by sentence

| Set | Sentence | Verdict |
|---|---|---|
| Visit touch 1, generic | "Your reader has had {BookTitle} …" | ⭐ **No change needed.** The subject of *has had* is the **reader**, who does not become plural when a second book arrives. Asserted, so the absence of a change is on the record rather than looking like an omission. |
| Visit touch 1, named | "{ChildFirstName} has had/have had {BookTitle} …" | ⭐ **No change needed.** Its verb already agrees with the **child** count via `bhp_review_ask_child_verb()` (1.19.369). |
| Web touch 1 | "… **It went out** in the mail, so I never got to see who opened **it**." | ⛔ **BROKEN by seal 1032** on a multi-book order. Repaired — see §6. |
| Touch 2 body | names no book at all | ⭐ **Nothing to pluralise.** See §7. |
| Touch 2 / all captions | "Tap a star to rate …" | Slot name only. |

New helper `bhp_review_ask_book_verb( $order, $singular, $plural )` — the exact
shape of `bhp_review_ask_child_verb()`, which has done this for child names since
1.19.369.

## 6. ⛔ THE ONE JUDGEMENT CALL, FLAGGED RATHER THAN SLIPPED THROUGH

The brief said: *"adjust only articles/verbs, never the approved wording."*
`it` → `they` and `it` → `them` are **PRONOUNS**, not articles or verbs.

**What ships on a two- or three-book web order:**

> "Your reader has had The Mariana Trench and Mount Everest for a couple of weeks
> now. **They** went out in the mail, so I never got to see who opened **them**."

**What 1.19.374 would have shipped:**

> "… The Mariana Trench and Mount Everest for a couple of weeks now. **It** went
> out in the mail, so I never got to see who opened **it**."

This desk judged the ungrammatical plural to be the worse of the two errors and
made the smallest change that fixes it. ⚠ **The call belongs to whoever owns the
copy.** The singular branch is **byte-identical to 1.19.374** and is still pinned
as V2 §4 verbatim by the suite, so a one-book parent reads exactly what Merry
wrote. **Reverting is one array literal** —
`inc\review-ask-email.php`, the `$mailed = bhp_review_ask_book_verb( … )` call at
the top of `bhp_review_ask_copy_web_touch1()`.

⛔ **`"Would you rate it?"` in the next paragraph was DELIBERATELY LEFT ALONE.**
Its `it` is the thing the star row rates, which seal 977 fixed at **one** book
and which 1.19.375 now **names** in the caption immediately below. *"Would you
rate them?"* would promise a row that can rate three books. **Open copy question
for Merry and Andrew, not an oversight.**

## 7. ⛔ Touch 2 — the brief named it, and there was nothing to do

The round-14 brief said the body sentence in *"touch 1 (visit and web) and touch
2"* must name every chapter book. **Touch 2's body names no book at all.** Merry's
V2 §3 body is *"I know how a week can get away from me, so I made this as short as
I could."* and its `body_after` is *"If it is not for you, that is completely
fine…"* — no `{BookTitle}` in either.

**Writing one in would have been minting customer-facing copy in a locked email
(Standing Rules §9).** It was not done. The only seal-1032 change to touch 2 is
its caption's slot name. §17 asserts **both** facts, so the absence is on the
record as a decision.

## 8. ⛔⛔ AN OPEN DEFECT FOUND, NOT CAUSED, AND NOT FIXED

`inc\visit-completed-email.php:407` — the **day-0** email, on a multi-book visit
order, renders:

> "I want to tell you why The Mariana Trench and Mount Everest **is** built the
> way **it is**, because **it is** built for one particular kid."

Three disagreements in one sentence, in front of a parent holding both books.

- ⚠ **NOT NEW and NOT caused by seal 1032.** `{BookTitle(s)}` has been the joined
  list in this lane since **1.19.364**. Rendering the round-14 fixtures is what
  exposed it.
- ⛔ **NOT FIXED HERE.** Repair needs `is`→`are`, `it is`→`they are` and
  `it`→`they` — three changes to **approved founder copy** in a lane the round-14
  brief did not name. Standing Rules §9 puts that with Andrew and Merry.
- ⭐ Commented in place at the call site with the rendered defect spelled out, so
  it cannot be lost. `bhp_review_ask_book_verb()` exists; the sentence is one
  `sprintf()` away.
- **Recommend as a round-15 item.**

