# ROUND 15 — 1.19.376 — seal 1042 receipt table + the day-0 plural sentence

**Aragorn (`lead-developer`) · 2026-09-05 · CYCLE179-LD-REVIEW-SEQ round 15 · lock `lead-developer-CYCLE179-LD-REVIEW-SEQ-R15.lock`**

## R15.1 Objective and acceptance criteria

1. **Seal 1042 (a)** — the day-0 receipt shipping row prints the pickup method
   name in BOTH cells. The `<th>` must carry only "Hand delivery:"; the `<td>`
   must carry the approved pickup label once.
2. **Seal 1042 (b)** — the ≤480px `word-break: break-word !important` applied to
   every `th`/`td` and split "Quantity", "Price" and "$11.99" mid-word. Scope
   `word-break` to the product-name cell; give the quantity and price columns
   width floors with `white-space: nowrap`.
3. **The round-14 open defect** at `inc/visit-completed-email.php` — a two- or
   three-book visit order rendered *"why A and B **is** built the way **it is**,
   because **it is** built…"*. Plural verbs and pronouns for two or more; the
   singular sentence stays verbatim.
4. Nothing else changes. Bump to 1.19.376.

## R15.2 ⛔⛔ THE DIAGNOSIS THAT CHANGED THE FIX — TWO RENDERS, NOT AN OPINION

1.19.374 already contained a `<th>` trim and it **did not reach the render**.
Rather than re-apply the same idea harder, the two renders on disk were read
byte-for-byte:

| | `rs373-day0.html` line 151 | `rs374-day0.html` line 151 |
|---|---|---|
| shipping `<th>` | `Hand delivery: Author hand-delivery at the Dallas Harris Elementary visit (September 3)` | **byte-identical** |
| shipping `<td>` | `Collection from <strong>…</strong>:<br>Andrew brings the signed books…` | `<div style="text-align: left;">Author hand-delivery at the Dallas Harris Elementary visit (September 3)</div>` |

So at priority 99 the callback **ran** (the `<td>` changed) and its **label write
did not survive**. The bundle plugin sets that label to exactly `Hand delivery:`
at priority 20 (`bhp_school_pickup_order_totals_label()`), and 373 — which had no
theme callback at all — still rendered the appended form. ⭐ **The only ordering
that explains both facts is a callback registered LATER than 99 that appends the
pickup location name to whatever label is present.** A trim therefore has to be
the last thing to touch the rows.

⚠ **NOT VERIFIED, AND IT IS THE FIRST THING TO CHECK:** the appending callback
has not been named or read — there is no PHP on this machine and the WooCommerce
source is not in this repo. The priority move is **derived from the two renders**,
not from reading the code that does the appending. **If the appending happens in
a template rather than in a filter, no priority can win and the `<th>` will still
be long on the 376 render.**

## R15.3 What was implemented

**(a) The row — `woocommerce\emails\customer-completed-order.php`**

`add_filter( 'woocommerce_get_order_item_totals', 'bhp_visit_email_shorten_pickup_row', PHP_INT_MAX, 2 )`
(was `99`), with the matching `remove_filter`. Still attached on the line before
`woocommerce_email_order_details` and detached on the line after, still only on
the visit fork — an ordinary web receipt never has it attached at any moment.

**(a) The label — `incisit-completed-email.php`**

The `<th>` is now written from `bhp_school_pickup_totals_label() . ':'` — the
bundle plugin's own single source for those words on all four surfaces — instead
of being carved out of the incoming label with `strpos`/`substr`. ⭐ This renders
**the same two words 1.19.374 rendered**; no copy is minted. It also trims a
label that arrives with **no colon**, which the 1.19.374 code could not. The
1.19.374 `substr` path is kept as the fallback for a store with the bundle plugin
inactive.

**(b) The CSS — `inc	ransactional-emails.php`**

| 1.19.374 | 1.19.376 |
|---|---|
| `th, td { … word-break: break-word !important; }` | `th, td { … }` — the blanket break is **gone** |
| — | `tr.order_item td.text-align-left { word-break: break-word !important; }` |
| — | `thead th.text-align-right, tr.order_item td.text-align-right, tr.order-totals td.text-align-right { white-space: nowrap !important; }` |

⭐ **Why `nowrap` is a width floor.** A table column cannot be narrower than the
widest unbreakable run inside it, so `×1`, `$11.99` and the words `Quantity` and
`Price` set the two right-hand columns and the product column takes the rest.

⛔ **The downloads table is deliberately excluded from the break.** Its link TEXT
wraps at its spaces; the long `?download_file=…` string is an `href` and never
renders. Reading the render shows the 1.19.374 downloads fix was the LEFT-ALIGN,
not the break — the 1.19.374 note credited it to the wrong rule.

⛔ **Every selector matches a real element, and that is a hard requirement.**
Emogrifier **prunes media rules whose selectors match nothing in the document**:
the 1.19.374 `tfoot th, tfoot td` pair is **missing from `rs374-day0.html` line
7** for exactly that reason (WooCommerce's totals block has no `<tfoot>`). That
pair is kept only because it costs nothing.

**(c) The plural sentence — `incisit-completed-email.php`**

The body paragraph becomes the `{WhyBuiltLine}` slot — the same idiom
`{VisitLine}` already uses in that array. Both forms live whole and greppable in
`bhp_visit_email_merge_values()` and are selected by `bhp_review_ask_book_verb()`,
the helper the review-ask lane has used since 1.19.375:

| Books | Rendered |
|---|---|
| 1 | *I want to tell you why {BookTitle(s)} **is** built the way **it is**, because **it is** built for one particular kid.* — **byte-identical to 1.19.375** |
| 2+ | *I want to tell you why {BookTitle(s)} **are** built the way **they are**, because **they are** built for one particular kid.* |

⛔ **The empty-title hard stop survives the move.** `{BookTitle(s)}` no longer
appears literally in that body, so `bhp_visit_email_merge_is_complete()` now also
requires `{WhyBuiltLine}`, which resolves to `''` when no title resolves. An
order with no book still refuses to send. The title is substituted **inside**
`{WhyBuiltLine}` rather than left to the outer `str_replace()`, because a later
slot cannot fill a token an earlier substitution introduced.

## R15.4 ⚠⚠ FOR ANDREW — A GRAMMAR-ONLY ADJUSTMENT TO APPROVED FOUNDER COPY

The plural branch changes `is`→`are`, `it is`→`they are` and `it`→`they`. **No
word is added and none is removed**, and the singular sentence every one-book
order receives is unchanged. It is built and reported as a grammar correction
**awaiting Andrew's confirmation**, not slipped in as an engineering detail.
⛔ Reverting it is one line: return the singular from the helper call in
`bhp_visit_email_merge_values()`.

